			"Message": "sync(Deps/Editor): Update to 6e18ef9e with Agent Host crash recovery\n\nUpdate the VS Code Editor dependency submodule from 9ef8f21 to 4878f46. This synchronization integrates critical stability improvements for the Agent Host lifecycle and terminal management, which are essential for the Cocoon extension host and Mountain backend operations.\n\nKey upstream changes include:\n- **Agent Host Phase 9:** Implemented crash recovery mechanisms that prevent permanent fatal latches, enabling robust subprocess restarts during live Claude sessions. Added support for abort, steering, and model hot-swapping.\n- **Terminal Reliability:** Fixed background terminal accumulation issues and enforced trust checks for local terminals within remote workspaces.\n- **Bug Fixes:** Resolved null guard issues in configuration trees, corrected off-by-one errors in extension pagination, and fixed protected modifier visibility in test helpers.\n- **UI Enhancements:** Enabled output renderers for chat code blocks and improved markdown frontmatter rendering.\n\nThis update ensures the editor maintains stability during complex agent operations and prevents indefinite hangs or UI corruption during extension lifecycle events.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
